edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186336484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338600 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b0492a08-2d29-5eca-af88-ac3ff00ea955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186337829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338641 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cac360d2-57d9-57d3-b6c0-afa920e3365f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339049 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339049 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339049 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339049 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339049 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "efbcfea6-0f26-55f3-9790-4f12e94364d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339049 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/7c/7c159c025f0b7ae4bfa8984f637a492cda21ec2dd39e87be724324e1334c06a3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339051 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339051 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339051 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339051 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339051 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9bfc53ce-85fd-5d88-8915-7ff8d8881ed6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339051 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/fe/fe16f5f3d1e9663a7e0df88d71639016bfb3357a6745ee6f125968978fd54c12.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339070 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339070 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339070 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339070 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339070 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f581ab20-43e5-59a8-ac58-914378a7361e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339070 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/6f/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/76/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373174 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373174 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72143" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373174 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373174 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/76/768046952484d181a404486547db84882424d98da4f677254484e1083580a39b.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373174 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef441fce-64e9-5f90-b9fb-0d44af6b333e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373174 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=y$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$ So, we have $0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/d5/d55cb7ea67d9865368c744577bb4a4b22a3635e8e62869ee65e945612d6c0e98.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=y$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt{y}.$ So, we have $y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373175 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "257fac2f-8a02-59c7-aca1-ef19cbb1795a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373176 #edb/ref 1080 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373176 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373176 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a975ac4-7eb7-5fd7-877f-3b02d86d178c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373177 #edb/ref 1080 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373177 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373177 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39895c7e-c47a-544c-91d0-9dfd7ed83606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373178 #edb/ref 1080 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373178 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373178 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a9081b22-1a7d-5fe6-a42e-28c78f31adb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373179 #edb/ref 1080 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373179 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373179 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cdc5c900-890c-5102-b2c4-66ae4d181695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373180 #edb/ref 1080 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373180 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373180 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ec0e614-7e69-564e-8bef-ca2ee0f86847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375294 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375294 #edb/ref 1075 